From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 06:55:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] perf(tauri): send the save over IPC in 8 MB chunks and
 rename it into place

On Windows every IPC request body is copied several times on its way to
the command (while one is in flight, WebView2's browser process commits
about 19 times its size and the Tauri host about 9.5 times), and wry
reads it on the window's UI thread. A save of tens of MB therefore
spiked memory by gigabytes and froze the window for the whole transfer.

saveDb() now writes database.bin through replaceFileInChunks(): the save
goes to database/database.bin.tmp in chunks of at most 8 MB (plugin-fs
write_file with append), and the temporary file is then renamed over
database.bin. If the rename fails (e.g. another program holds
database.bin open on Windows), the temporary file is copied over it.

The temporary file also keeps database.bin whole when a save is cut
short. RisuSaveDecoder skips blocks it cannot read, so a truncated
database.bin still loads, without the characters after the cut, and the
loader never falls back to a backup.

